prompt:
A Fabrikam Bicep file creates a public IP address and returns its resource ID. The security team wants the public IP address to be optional for private test deployments.

Current file:

```bicep
param location string = resourceGroup().location

resource pip 'Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses@2025-01-01' = {
  name: 'pip-web'
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard'
  }
  properties: {
    publicIPAllocationMethod: 'Static'
  }
}

output publicIpId string = pip.id
```

Which two changes should you make so deployment succeeds whether the public IP address is deployed or skipped? Each correct answer presents part of the solution. Select TWO.

options.text:
Add a Boolean parameter and apply an `if` expression to the public IP resource declaration.

```bicep
param deployPublicIp bool = true

resource pip 'Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses@2025-01-01' = if (deployPublicIp) {
  name: 'pip-web'
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard'
  }
  properties: {
    publicIPAllocationMethod: 'Static'
  }
}
```

Leave the resource unconditional and put `if (deployPublicIp)` inside the `properties` object.

```bicep
properties: if (deployPublicIp) {
  publicIPAllocationMethod: 'Static'
}
```

